From 7cb5b7e1c9c37df01d102996d186320188bc9430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:44:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: an output missing beside the other outputs of its
 card stays

An output that the engine did not list in this start was replaced, in
memory, by the output that Kodi validates it to when that has the same
card name, else by the output that the sink falls back to; and a missing
HDMI output followed the only output with a display. The name of the
card does not tell the outputs of a card apart: the four HDMI outputs of
an NVIDIA card are all "HDA NVidia". An output that was not listed only
because it could not be opened then (in use while the outputs were
listed, an UnconfigureSink() that ran out its 2 s, the instant of a
change of the display mode) was replaced by another output of the same
card, another display (a monitor on the PC of the user), until the
outputs were listed again; and Kodi's own validation, when it starts,
saved such an output in the setting, as the same device.

An output now belongs to a family, its kind on its card
(INTERNAL::OutputFamily(): "hdmi:NVidia" for "hdmi:CARD=NVidia,DEV=0",
"@:PCH" for the analog output of a laptop's sound chip; the friendly
name where a name has no card). A configured output that is not listed
while other outputs of its family are is a port of a card that is there:
it stays the output, it is tried as it is (when the sink cannot open it,
it falls back as Kodi's sink always did), it is not followed to another
output with a display, and ValidateOutputDevices() neither validates it
to another output of that card nor saves that in the setting. An output
whose family is not there at all (the HDMI output of integrated graphics
that are off, beside the analog output of the same chip; a card that is
gone) is followed away from, or replaced by the output that the sink
falls back to, as before. The engine says once which of the two it did.

Host tests (TestActiveAEFollowDisplay): the families, and the case of
the review with the outputs of the user's PC, which fails with the code
before (the TV's output replaced by a monitor's, followed to it); nine
more mutations make them fail.
